      "source": [
        "### Derivation from equilibrium\n",
        "\n",
        "Vertical equilibrium of the differential element gives\n",
        "\n",
        "\\[\n",
        "V-(V+dV)+w\\,dy=0\n",
        "\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n",
        "\\frac{dV}{dy}=-w\n",
        "\\]\n",
        "\n",
        "for the adopted sign convention. Moment equilibrium, after neglecting products of two infinitesimals, gives\n",
        "\n",
        "\\[\n",
        "\\frac{dM}{dy}=-V.\n",
        "\\]\n",
        "\n",
        "Integrating inward from the free-tip boundary conditions (V(L)=M(L)=0) produces the integral equations above. The signs depend on convention; the magnitudes and physical equilibrium do not."
      ],
      "id": "YhH3TTY05TF8"
    },
    {
