    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "EfvfcWX65TF-"
      },
      "source": [
        "For a single closed cell, equilibrium gives the nearly constant shear flow (q=T/(2A_m)). Wall shear stress is (\tau=q/t), so thinner walls experience greater shear stress. Compatibility around the cell then produces (J) and the twist rate (T/(GJ)). This is why closing a wing box dramatically improves torsional stiffness compared with an open channel."
      ],
      "id": "EfvfcWX65TF-"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "g9s2cb9G5TF_"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "#@title 5A. Compute torque and twist { display-mode: \"form\" }\n",
        "OFFSET_E_MM = 25.0 #@param {type:\"number\"}\n",
        "TWIST_LIMIT_DEG = 3.0 #@param {type:\"number\"}\n",
        "e=OFFSET_E_MM*1e-3; Gmat=G_GPA*1e9\n",
        "Bm=B-tw; Hm=H-tf; Am=Bm*Hm\n",
        "J=4*Am**2/(2*Bm/tf+2*Hm/tw)\n",
        "mt=e*w\n",
        "T=integrate_from_tip(mt,y)\n",
        "phi=cumtrapz_from_root(T/(Gmat*J),y)\n",
        "fig,axs=plt.subplots(1,2,figsize=(12,4))\n",
        "axs[0].plot(y,T,lw=3); axs[0].set(xlabel=\"y [m]\",ylabel=\"T [N m]\",title=\"Internal torque\")\n",
        "axs[1].plot(y,np.degrees(phi),lw=3,color=\"#8e44ad\"); axs[1].set(xlabel=\"y [m]\",ylabel=\"twist [deg]\",title=\"Elastic twist\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n",
        "print(f\"Thin-wall torsion constant J = {J*1e12:.2f} mm⁴\")\n",
        "print(f\"Tip twist = {np.degrees(phi[-1]):.5f} deg; limit = {TWIST_LIMIT_DEG:.3f} deg\")"
      ],
      "id": "g9s2cb9G5TF_"
    },
